{"id":"a509dc7d83554231abf638054f2764650f6ca2f2","axis":"silent","repo":"pnpm/pnpm","sha":"a509dc7d83554231abf638054f2764650f6ca2f2","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/custom-resolution-integrity-reimports.md","lines":["@@ -2,4 +2,4 @@"," \"pacquet\": patch"," ---"," ","-`pnpm install` now re-fetches a package from a custom resolver when the `integrity` of its resolution changes. It used to update the lockfile but keep the old files in `node_modules`. Installs with `enableGlobalVirtualStore` still keep the old files [#15670](https://github.com/pnpm/pnpm/issues/15670).","+`pnpm install` now re-fetches a package from a custom resolver when the `integrity` of its resolution changes, with or without `enableGlobalVirtualStore`. It used to update the lockfile but keep the old files in `node_modules` [#15670](https://github.com/pnpm/pnpm/issues/15670)."],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/cli/tests/suite/custom_resolvers.rs","lines":["@@ -652,6 +652,18 @@ module.exports = {{"," /// Regression test for pnpm/pnpm#15670."," #[test]"," fn changed_custom_resolution_integrity_re_imports_the_package() {","+    assert_changed_custom_integrity_reinstalls(false);","+}","+","+/// A global-virtual-store slot is named by a hash of the package id, so a","+/// custom integrity has to be part of that id for the new bytes to get a","+/// slot of their own (pnpm/pnpm#15670).","+#[test]","+fn changed_custom_resolution_integrity_re_imports_the_package_into_the_global_virtual_store() {","+    assert_changed_custom_integrity_reinstalls(true);","+}","+","+fn assert_changed_custom_integrity_reinstalls(global_virtual_store: bool) {","     let CommandTempCwd {","         pacquet,","         root,","@@ -669,6 +681,9 @@ fn changed_custom_resolution_integrity_re_imports_the_package() {","     };","     fs::write(workspace.join(\"package.json\"), r#\"{\"dependencies\":{\"dep-a\":\"1.0.0\"}}\"#).unwrap();","     crate::_utils::append_workspace_yaml_key(&workspace, \"